{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>May He remember</b> — the meaning: why will He help you? For He will remember all your meal-offerings, and this is what is written in the Torah: \"And you shall sound the trumpets and you shall be remembered and you shall be saved.\" And some say: burnt-offerings were offered at the time of wars, as in \"and I will prepare and I will bring up the burnt-offering.\"" "<b>Will make fat</b> — the fire of the altar will burn it and it will turn to ashes." "And the word ידשנה — like ואקראה לך, in that the alef does not come kamatz-gadol as is the rule with the addition of the heh; therefore many say that they resemble quadriliteral roots."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:58.229476510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}